>Settling raw water quick card
Settle muddy water in a marked raw container.
Pour the clearer layer into a second raw container, stopping before sediment moves. Strain through a clean cloth or coffee filter if needed. Keep raw gear away from clean bottle mouths. Straining leaves germs and dissolved chemicals. Boil or use suitable treatment for germs; reject suspected chemical pollution.

